Build QEMU as an embeddable shared library per softmmu target
(libqemu-embed-<target>), from the existing per-target static lib plus
embed/libqemu_embed.c (overlaid by scripts/prepare-qemu.sh). Objects are
linked directly so type_init constructors survive. Needs -fPIC
(scripts/configure-qemu.sh). Design: docs/11-m1-embed-api.md

It links the target's stubs archive (`target_stubs`, QEMU 11) as the
emulators do: without it the aarch64 library on a host with no KVM is
left with KVM's symbols undefined (`_kvm_arm_pmu_init`, ...).

On Windows (2026-09-06, M11) it also compiles hw/mesa/mglcntx_mingw.c a
second time, with MESAGL_WGL_BACKEND, into the emulators alone: that file
holds both the WGL backend and the helpers every backend needs, the
static library is shared object-for-object with this shared library, and
the embed library brings its own window-less backend. See patch 31 for
why weak symbols do not do this job on COFF.

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index cf78c54596..2a5da02834 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -4415,6 +4415,40 @@ foreach target : target_dirs
                  c_args: c_args,
                  build_by_default: false)
 
+  # win98-xp-virt: QEMU as an embeddable shared library (embed/libqemu_embed.h)
+  if target.endswith('-softmmu')
+    shared_library('qemu-embed-' + target_name,
+                   files('embed/libqemu_embed.c', 'embed/embedaudio.c', 'embed/embedfx.c', 'embed/mglcntx_embed.c'),
+                   c_args: c_args,
+                   include_directories: target_inc,
+                   dependencies: arch_deps + [target_stubs] + (opengl.found() ? [opengl] : []) + (gbm.found() ? [gbm] : []),
+                   objects: lib.extract_all_objects(recursive: true),
+                   link_depends: [block_syms, qemu_syms],
+                   # macOS: emulator_link_args carries -exported_symbols_list for the
+                   # TCG plugin API only; add ours (ld64 merges multiple lists).
+                   link_args: link_args + (host_os == 'darwin' ?
+                     ['-Wl,-exported_symbols_list,' + meson.current_source_dir() / 'embed/libqemu_embed.symbols'] : []),
+                   install: true)
+  endif
+
+  # 2ksbox: the Mesa pass-through's WGL backend, for the emulators only.
+  # `lib` above is shared object-for-object with libqemu-embed, which
+  # brings its own window-less backend (embed/mglcntx_embed.c), so the two
+  # cannot both be in there. hw/mesa/mglcntx_mingw.c is compiled once more
+  # here with MESAGL_WGL_BACKEND, which is its backend half alone (its
+  # other half, the platform-independent helpers, stays in `lib` where
+  # both consumers get it).
+  mesa_wgl_objects = []
+  if host_os == 'windows'
+    mesa_wgl = static_library('mesa-wgl-' + target_name,
+                              files('hw/mesa/mglcntx_mingw.c'),
+                              dependencies: lib_deps,
+                              include_directories: target_inc + [include_directories('hw/mesa')],
+                              c_args: c_args + ['-DMESAGL_WGL_BACKEND'],
+                              build_by_default: false)
+    mesa_wgl_objects = mesa_wgl.extract_all_objects(recursive: false)
+  endif
+
   if target.endswith('-softmmu')
     execs = [{
       'name': 'qemu-system-' + target_name,
@@ -4457,7 +4491,7 @@ foreach target : target_dirs
                install: true,
                c_args: c_args,
                dependencies: arch_deps + exe['dependencies'],
-               objects: lib.extract_all_objects(recursive: true),
+               objects: [lib.extract_all_objects(recursive: true), mesa_wgl_objects],
                link_depends: [block_syms, qemu_syms],
                link_args: link_args,
                win_subsystem: exe['win_subsystem'])
